&lt;p&gt;Then the &lt;b&gt;domain&lt;/b&gt; of the relation is the set of first coordinates of the elements of \(R\), so,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-left: 30px"&gt;\(\text{Dom}(R) = \{a \in A : (a,b) \in R\} \)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Similarly, the &lt;b&gt;range&lt;/b&gt; of the relation is the set of second coordinates of the elements of \(R\), so,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-left: 30px"&gt;\(\text{Range}(R) = \{b \in B : (a,b) \in R\)&lt;/p&gt;</text>
